Begin Exploring Related Columns
column name: potential usage
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."cpc": holds Cooperative Patent Classification data; flatten it to locate symbols that start with ‘A61%’.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."assignee_harmonized": array‑variant that contains standardized assignee names; flatten it to pull each name out.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."filing_date": numeric yyyymmdd; derive filing year with e.g. TO_VARCHAR("filing_date")[1,4] or INT("filing_date"/10000).  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."publication_number": helps view individual records while exploring data.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."application_number": unique application key, used when counting “applications”.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."family_id": can be used to de‑duplicate simple families if necessary.  
Conditions that may be useful  
• LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."cpc") f — to explode CPC array.  
• WHERE f.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%' — keep only A61 category.  
• LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."assignee_harmonized") a — to explode assignee array.  
• WHERE a.value:"name"::STRING IS NOT NULL — ignore empty names.  
• INT(t."filing_date"/10000) AS "filing_year" — obtain 4‑digit year for grouping.  



```sql
--Description: Peek into CPC objects to understand their structure
SELECT p."publication_number",
       f.value AS cpc_raw
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Show distinct CPC symbols that start with “A61” to confirm filter works
SELECT DISTINCT f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS cpc_symbol
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
WHERE  f.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Sample publications that carry at least one A61 CPC code
SELECT p."publication_number",
       LISTAGG(DISTINCT f.value:"symbol"::STRING, ', ') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY f.value:"symbol"::STRING) AS a61_symbols
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
WHERE  f.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
GROUP  BY p."publication_number"
LIMIT 20;
```

